From ccbcec58c29d19d4879025fabdeb0c829faf3131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:03:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/32] codegen: emit a spin-wait hint for db16cyc

db16cyc (or r31,r31,r31, a Xenon 16-cycle delay hint) sits in guest
spin-wait loops and was dropped, so those loops spun at full speed. Emit
simde_mm_pause() instead: PAUSE on x86, YIELD/ISB on ARM. A spinning
thread draws less power and leaves its core to the SMT sibling.

Xenia Canary does the same: ppc_emit_alu.cc InstrEmit_orx turns
0x7FFFFB78 into DelayExecution, which x64_sequences.cc DELAY_EXECUTION
emits as pause (its comment: "heavily used in spinlocks. since we do not
emit any code for this we end up wasting a ton of power").

Measured in Project Gotham Racing 4 on a Steam Deck OLED under Proton
(pgr4-native README, scripted St Petersburg race,
td-81 against td-79): race 84.8 fps (83.4), 1 % low 55.7 (55.5).

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/codegen/builders/system.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/codegen/builders/system.cpp b/src/codegen/builders/system.cpp
index f560429..04f3292 100644
--- a/src/codegen/builders/system.cpp
+++ b/src/codegen/builders/system.cpp
@@ -61,8 +61,9 @@ bool build_eieio(BuilderContext& ctx) {
 }
 
 bool build_db16cyc(BuilderContext& ctx) {
-  // Xenon-specific 16-cycle delay hint, no effect in recompiled code
-  (void)ctx;
+  // Xenon's 16-cycle delay hint sits in spin-wait loops. PAUSE is the host's spin-wait hint: the
+  // loop draws less power and leaves the core to its SMT sibling.
+  ctx.println("\tsimde_mm_pause();");
   return true;
 }
 
